        "original_id": "70af29f0-6c70-5c50-8164-bb6c8f0fcde6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: João Paulo II Airport, São Miguel, Azores\n- Organizations: SATA Group, SATA Air Açores, Azores Airlines, Ryanair\n- People: Pope John Paul II\n- Topics: airport hubs, airline traffic rankings\n\nFacts:\n- João Paulo II Airport is an international airport on the island of São Miguel in the Portuguese archipelago of the Azores.\n- João Paulo II Airport is named after Pope John Paul II.\n- João Paulo II Airport has the codes IATA: PDL and ICAO: LPPD.\n- João Paulo II Airport is the major hub for the SATA Group of airlines.\n- The SATA Group includes SATA Air Açores for inter-island service and Azores Airlines for international service.\n- Since April 2015, Ryanair has operated a base at João Paulo II Airport.\n- In 2016, Ryanair was the largest European airline by scheduled passengers flown.\n- In 2016, Ryanair carried more international passengers than any other airline.",
